  "rootCause": "Cointelegraph reported that on November 2, a project called Axion Network launched the token AXN and was hacked a few hours after it was hacked. 79 billion AXN were minted and sold to the market. The token price was almost zero. The hacker made a profit of 1,300 ETH, or about $500,000.",
  "descriptions": [
    {
      "source": "SlowMist",
      "text": "Cointelegraph reported that on November 2, a project called Axion Network launched the token AXN and was hacked a few hours after it was hacked. 79 billion AXN were minted and sold to the market. The token price was almost zero. The hacker made a profit of 1,300 ETH, or about $500,000."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "Axion’s Ethereum launch was broken on 2020-11-02 by an infinite-mint exploit that minted 79.228 billion AXN, sold the tokens for 1,309.726383687296628968 ETH, and left a reported loss near $500,000. A deployment-time code injection in the Axion staking contract’s OpenZeppelin AccessControl dependency let the unstake path mint AXN without a backing stake."
    }
  ],
